       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults, and a single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. The risks at that level include GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum prescription dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO every 4\u20136 hours as needed** for mild to moderate pain. This would be 4 doses a day at most, or 1,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter that. If the pain control needs are higher, a multimodal approach might help, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen.\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and any note for the order, such as the indication or \"take with food.\""
